      "writtenOn": "2022-03-10T22:05:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we can change A13\u0027s GKI default console behavior this late, but how about this alternative suggestion?\n\nWe enable CONFIG_NULL_TTY in GKI, and QC sets \"console\u003dttynull\" in their bootloader or vendor_boot.img by default, and then your perf team can either drop this flag or leave it and just add console\u003dttyXX for enabling debugging?\n\nIn A14 we\u0027d also add \"console\u003dttynull\" to gki_defconfig which eliminates some complexity for QC.\n\nLet me know if this alternative can work, as it would avoid a bit more out of tree code. If it doesn\u0027t, please think about it for A14 so we can drop this.",
      "parentUuid": "c0af89f5_ad75d1c1",
      "revId": "4c571f456085d9f1c10611a58352dc00e95e7a3d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
