      "writtenOn": "2022-03-10T22:43:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We enable CONFIG_NULL_TTY in GKI, and QC sets \"console\u003dttynull\" in their bootloader or vendor_boot.img by default, and then your perf team can either drop this flag or leave it and just add console\u003dttyXX for enabling debugging?\n\nThis approach doesn\u0027t work well for us because bootloader doesn\u0027t know whether it is loading a \"perf\" or \"debug\" image. The only code which knows between the 2 is the kernel itself and a few userspace scripts to enable extra tracing. Devicetree and bootloader behaves the same between perf and debug builds.",
      "parentUuid": "68445b7d_d3c7798b",
      "revId": "4c571f456085d9f1c10611a58352dc00e95e7a3d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
