      "writtenOn": "2022-03-10T23:02:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another piece of this I didn\u0027t understand yet. It looks like the printk code will only print messages to your console if it passes the try_enable_new_console() check, and that\u0027s looking for e.g. \"console\u003dttyMSMx\" on the cmdline. It could also happen if somebody had called add_preferred_console(), or the console driver registered with CON_CONSDEV. But I know geni doesn\u0027t use that flag, or call add_preferred_console() itself. So is this kernel patch really just about \"ignoring\" the console\u003dttyMSMx your bootloader always adds to the cmdline? If so, that seems like a bit of a hack, doesn\u0027t it?",
      "parentUuid": "15d98f4d_99a7e36a",
